  subject: Record&lt;string,string&gt;;
  statement: string;
  contract_root: string;
}
</code>
<p>The exact claim ID is part of proof identity. Evidence for another addre=
ss/account/handle cannot satisfy it.</p>



5. Evidence must prove provenance, not just bytes
<p>The current <code>sha256(evidence_string)</code> model is insufficient. =
It proves only that bytes were hashed.</p>
<p>Every evidence item needs structured provenance:</p>

<code>interface Evidence {
  id: string;                  // content-addressed
  class: string;               // registrar_readback, dns_answer, smtp_chal=
lenge, etc
  claim_id: string;

  observed_at: string;
  source: string;              // provider / DNS authority / mailbox / publ=
ic endpoint
  locator: string;             // sanitized canonical source locator

  collector_id: string;
  collector_program_hash: string;
  collector_runtime_hash: string;

  request_hash?: string;
  response_hash: string;
  normalized_payload_hash: string;

  nonce?: string;
  independence_group: string;

  signature?: string;
  signer?: string;
}
</code>
<p>Evidence payload bytes go into content-addressed blob storage. Canonical=
 proof state stores hashes/metadata, not mutable arbitrary strings.</p>
<p>Required invariant:</p>

<code>hash(bytes) is not provenance
</code>
<p>For important external effects, provider acknowledgement and independent=
 readback should be different evidence classes / independence groups where =
feasible.</p>
<p>Same-channel acknowledgement is usually not enough to establish an exter=
nally persistent fact.</p>



6. Judges must be content-addressed deterministic programs
<p>A gate name such as <code>handle_owned_v1</code> means nothing unless it=
 resolves to immutable program bytes.</p>
<p>Create a registry:</p>

<code>interface ProgramBundle {
  id: string;
  source_hash: string;
  runtime_hash: string;
  config_hash: string;
  dependency_hash: string;
  bundle_hash: string;
}
</code>
<p>A proof pins <code>bundle_hash</code>, not only a friendly name.</p>
<p>Judges must be pure over canonical evidence input. No network calls insi=
de judges. Network observations happen in probes/collectors before judgment=
.</p>

<code>judge(evidence: CanonicalEvidenceSet): ActualityResult
</code>
<p>A judge should return structured reasons and evidence IDs used.</p>



7. Authority is a different object from truth
<p>Delete the mental model that <code>confirmed:true</code> is authority.</=
p>
<p>A consequential effect requires a bounded signed grant/ticket issued bef=
ore the effect.</p>
<p>Suggested object:</p>

<code>interface Grant {
  protocol: &quot;qp/1&quot;;
  id: string;

  issuer: string;        // human:&lt;public-key-id&gt; or trusted policy i=
ssuer
  subject: string;       // agent/session principal

  action: string;        // cf.domain.register, telnyx.number.purchase, ema=
il.send, etc
  payload_hash: string;  // exact effect payload

  constraints: {
    max_amount?: number;
    currency?: string;
    provider?: string;
    resource?: string;
    scopes?: string[];
  };

  issued_at: string;
  expires_at: string;
  nonce: string;
  max_uses: 1;

  signature: string;
}
</code>
<p>Use Ed25519 or equivalent modern deterministic signing.</p>
<p>Grant validation requires:</p>

<code>signature valid
issuer trusted by policy
subject matches executor
exact action matches
exact payload hash matches
constraints satisfied
not expired
nonce not consumed
remaining uses &gt; 0
</code>
<p>After reserve/consumption, replay of the same grant must fail.</p>
<p>Never infer authority from a true claim.</p>
<p>Example:</p>

<code>domain_available(privately.win) =3D=3D TRUE
</code>
<p>does NOT imply:</p>

<code>agent may purchase privately.win
</code>
<p>The first is truth. The second requires =CE=9B.</p>



8. Consequential action lifecycle
<p>For money, sends, DNS writes, account writes, OAuth grants, credential c=
hanges, posting, etc., enforce:</p>

<code>AUTHORIZE -&gt; RESERVE -&gt; ACT -&gt; INDEPENDENT READBACK -&gt; SE=
TTLE
</code>
<p>Not:</p>

<code>ACT -&gt; trust provider response -&gt; mark done
</code>
<p>Detailed sequence:</p>
<ol>
<li>Build exact proposed effect payload.</li>
<li>Hash canonical payload.</li>
<li>Validate signed grant against exact payload hash.</li>
<li>Atomically reserve the grant/budget/idempotency key.</li>
<li>Execute provider adapter once.</li>
<li>Persist provider response as evidence, but do not settle target claim y=
et.</li>
<li>Run independent readback/challenge probe.</li>
<li>Normalize evidence.</li>
<li>Run pinned judges and gates.</li>
<li>If Actuality=3DTRUE and all gates pass, settle TransitionReceipt.</li>
<li>Reconcile reservation/spend.</li>
<li>Mark grant consumed.</li>
<li>Project resulting canonical state into tasks/UI.</li>
</ol>
<p>If readback fails or is unavailable:</p>

<code>NO successful target-state receipt
Actuality =3D UNKNOWN
</code>
<p>The effect may have happened, so retain an effect-attempt receipt and sc=
hedule reconciliation, but do not lie about the target claim.</p>



9. TransitionReceipt
<p>Implement one canonical receipt object and use it everywhere.</p>
<p>Suggested shape:</p>

<code>interface TransitionReceipt {
  protocol: &quot;qp/1&quot;;
  transition_type: &quot;RESOLVE&quot; | &quot;EFFECT&quot; | &quot;REVOKE&=
quot;;

  contract_root: string;
  claim_id: string;

  state_before_root: string;
  proposal_root: string;

  evidence_root: string;
  judge_results_root: string;
  gate_results_root: string;

  actuality: &quot;TRUE&quot; | &quot;FALSE&quot; | &quot;UNKNOWN&quot;;

  authority_id?: string;
  authority_root?: string;

  transition_program_hash: string;
  state_after_root: string;

  run: {
    executor_id: string;
    program_hash: string;
    runtime_hash: string;
    started_at: string;
    finished_at: string;
    cost?: number;
  };

  prev_receipt_hash: string;
  settled_at: string;

  receipt_hash: string;
  qp_signer: string;
  qp_signature: string;
}
</code>
<p>No mutable random <code>PRF-...</code> ID as the canonical identity. The=
 canonical receipt identity is the content hash of canonical receipt bytes =
excluding/appropriately handling the signature field.</p>
<p>Receipts are append-only. Never overwrite <code>cap.proof</code>.</p>



10. Replay / settlement verifier
<p>Implement a second verification path that can take only:</p>
<ul>
<li>ProofSpec / ContractRoot bundle</li>
<li>claim</li>
<li>evidence blobs + provenance</li>
<li>judge/gate program bundles</li>
<li>authority object if required</li>
<li>previous state root</li>
<li>TransitionReceipt</li>
</ul>
<p>and independently recompute:</p>
<ul>
<li>hashes</li>
<li>freshness at historical <code>settled_at</code></li>
<li>evidence admissibility</li>
<li>actuality</li>
<li>gate outcomes</li>
<li>authority validity/consumption semantics</li>
<li>transition result</li>
<li>resulting state root</li>
<li>receipt hash/signature</li>
</ul>
<p>It must return <code>PASS | FAIL</code>, never silently repair the recei=
pt.</p>
<p>Canonical proof requires replay <code>PASS</code>.</p>



11. Exact cmail ProofSpecs
<p>Implement the following first. These are the root proofs from which setu=
p.social can safely expand.</p>

P1 =E2=80=94 domain_available(provider, domain)
<p>Claim:</p>

<code>The named registrar/provider currently reports exact domain D as regi=
strable under the requested product/tier.
</code>
<p>Evidence:</p>
<ul>
<li>authenticated registrar availability read</li>
<li>exact domain</li>
<li>account/provider context</li>
<li>price/currency/tier if returned</li>
<li>observation timestamp</li>
</ul>
<p>TRUE:</p>
<ul>
<li>provider explicitly returns registrable/available for exact domain and =
freshness window valid.</li>
</ul>
<p>FALSE:</p>
<ul>
<li>provider explicitly returns not registrable/taken for exact domain.</li=
>
</ul>
<p>UNKNOWN:</p>
<ul>
<li>timeout, auth error, malformed response, unsupported TLD, rate limit, m=
issing credentials, ambiguous provider response.</li>
</ul>
<p>Do not use DNS NXDOMAIN as TRUE. DNS can be supporting evidence only.</p=
>
<p>No authority required because this is read-only.</p>



P2 =E2=80=94 domain_owned(provider, account, domain)
<p>Claim:</p>

<code>Domain D is present as an owned/managed registration in expected regi=
strar account A.
</code>
<p>Evidence:</p>
<ul>
<li>post-effect authenticated registrar list/read endpoint</li>
<li>exact domain</li>
<li>expected account context</li>
<li>provider registration ID/state</li>
</ul>
<p>TRUE:</p>
<ul>
<li>independent authenticated readback returns D in expected account with a=
n acceptable registered/active state.</li>
</ul>
<p>FALSE:</p>
<ul>
<li>authoritative readback proves D belongs elsewhere / is not in expected =
account where provider semantics make this decidable.</li>
</ul>
<p>UNKNOWN:</p>
<ul>
<li>provider API unavailable, eventual consistency period, auth failure, am=
biguous state.</li>
</ul>
<p>For purchase transition, authority REQUIRED:</p>

<code>action =3D cf.domain.register
payload_hash =3D H({domain, provider, max_price/currency/contact policy/...=
})
</code>
<p>Provider POST success alone is not enough to settle <code>domain_owned</=
code>.</p>



P3 =E2=80=94 dns_configured(domain, expected_config)
<p>Claim:</p>

<code>Authoritative DNS for D matches frozen expected configuration C.
</code>
<p>Evidence:</p>
<ul>
<li>provider DNS config readback</li>
<li>independent authoritative DNS queries</li>
<li>expected record set hash</li>
</ul>
<p>TRUE only when required records match exact expected values.</p>
<p>FALSE when authoritative responses contradict required values after prop=
agation policy allows a decisive result.</p>
<p>UNKNOWN during propagation window, timeout, SERVFAIL, provider outage, e=
tc.</p>
<p>Do not conflate this with domain ownership.</p>



P4 =E2=80=94 email_route_configured(address, worker)
<p>Claim:</p>

<code>Exact address A is covered by an enabled routing rule whose action ta=
rgets expected worker W.
</code>
<p>Evidence:</p>
<ul>
<li>authenticated Cloudflare routing rules readback</li>
<li>exact rule / catch-all matcher</li>
<li>enabled state</li>
<li>exact worker action target</li>
</ul>
<p>TRUE only if matcher AND enabled AND action destination all match.</p>
<p>Current <code>verify-capacity.sh</code> is insufficient because it can p=
ass when routing rules exist without proving the intended worker target.</p=
>



P5 =E2=80=94 email_receives(address)
<p>This is the canonical inbound-email proof. EVP-1 should be rewritten to =
emit this QP proof.</p>
<p>Claim:</p>

<code>Exact address A can receive a fresh externally originated message thr=
ough the configured production route and expose it to cmail.
</code>
<p>Evidence requirements:</p>
<ol>
<li>prerequisite proofs <code>dns_configured</code> and <code>email_route_c=
onfigured</code> TRUE</li>
<li>QP-generated cryptographically random nonce N</li>
<li>independent sender sends a message containing N to exact A</li>
<li>cmail receives/indexes it</li>
<li>probe queries exact mailbox A, not a global search</li>
<li>evidence includes provider/raw message ID, target mailbox, sender, time=
stamps and raw-message hash</li>
</ol>
<p>TRUE:</p>
<ul>
<li>nonce N is observed in exact mailbox A within frozen timeout/freshness =
bounds and message evidence correlates to the challenge.</li>
</ul>
<p>FALSE:</p>
<ul>
<li>only when the ProofSpec=E2=80=99s bounded challenge protocol produces a=
 decisive delivery failure/bounce that proves the claim false.</li>
</ul>
<p>UNKNOWN:</p>
<ul>
<li>timeout without a decisive negative, sender failure, probe failure, glo=
bal system outage, ambiguous delivery.</li>
</ul>
<p>Critical: the current <code>verify-email.sh roundtrip</code> accepts <co=
de>&lt;mailbox&gt;</code> but globally searches by token. Fix it. Receipt e=
vidence must bind token to exact mailbox.</p>
<p>Infrastructure 1-7 green is <code>DEGRADED/CONFIGURED</code>, not <code>=
CERTIFIED</code> for receive capability. Only round-trip settles <code>emai=
l_receives=3DTRUE</code>.</p>



P6 =E2=80=94 phone_owned(provider, account, number)
<p>Claim:</p>

<code>Exact phone number N is provisioned in expected provider account A an=
d is in an acceptable active state.
</code>
<p>Evidence:</p>
<ul>
<li>authenticated Telnyx read/list response after purchase</li>
<li>exact number</li>
<li>provider resource ID</li>
<li>account identity</li>
<li>status</li>
</ul>
