<p>Account creation UI completion is not itself proof of ownership.</p>



P10 =E2=80=94 handle_bound(platform, account_id, handle)
<p>Claim:</p>

<code>Owned account ID is currently publicly bound to exact handle H.
</code>
<p>Prerequisite:</p>

<code>account_owned(platform, account_id) =3D=3D TRUE
</code>
<p>Evidence:</p>
<ul>
<li>authenticated account profile readback</li>
<li>public profile/identity readback where useful</li>
</ul>
<p>TRUE only when exact account ID and handle reconcile.</p>
<p>This replaces the current broken <code>have_handle</code> verifier.</p>



P11 =E2=80=94 oauth_authorized(provider, principal, scope_set)
<p>Claim:</p>

<code>Controlled principal has an active authorization/token grant containi=
ng at least exact required scope set S.
</code>
<p>Evidence:</p>
<ul>
<li>provider token introspection or authenticated test call(s)</li>
<li>token credential itself stays secret; evidence stores credential refere=
nce/hash, never raw token</li>
<li>exact normalized scope set</li>
<li>expiry/revocation data if available</li>
</ul>
<p>TRUE only when provider evidence proves required scopes.</p>
<p>OAuth consent UI success text alone is not canonical proof.</p>



P12 =E2=80=94 can_post(platform, account_id)
<p>Do not infer <code>can_post</code> merely from account ownership or OAut=
h existence.</p>
<p>Claim:</p>

<code>Current controlled authorization for account ID permits the frozen wr=
ite operation class.
</code>
<p>Preferred proof:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>account_owned =3D=3D TRUE</code></li>
<li><code>oauth_authorized(required_write_scopes) =3D=3D TRUE</code></li>
