P13 =E2=80=94 email_send_accepted / email_delivered
<p>Split these claims.</p>
<p><code>email_send_accepted(message)</code>:</p>
<ul>
<li>provider/SENDER accepted exact message payload and returned canonical p=
rovider ID.</li>
</ul>
<p><code>email_delivered(message)</code>:</p>
<ul>
<li>independent downstream receipt/bounce/controlled inbox readback proves =
delivery according to the ProofSpec.</li>
</ul>
<p>Current <code>message_id &amp;&amp; delivery_status !=3D failed</code> i=
s not enough to prove delivery.</p>
<p>Sending requires signed exact-payload authority.</p>



12. Replace the current GRANT graph with typed edges
<p>Do not call every dependency edge a grant.</p>
<p>Use at least:</p>

<code>type EdgeKind =3D
  | &quot;REQUIRES&quot;
  | &quot;DERIVES&quot;
  | &quot;ENABLES&quot;
  | &quot;AUTHORIZES&quot;
  | &quot;EFFECTS&quot;
  | &quot;VERIFIES&quot;;
</code>
<p>Examples:</p>

<code>domain_owned(D) ENABLES task configure_dns(D)
email_receives(A) ENABLES task signup(platform,A)
account_owned(P,ID) REQUIRES oauth_authorized(P,principal,S) for some write=
s
signed Grant AUTHORIZES cf.domain.register(payload_hash)
provider effect EFFECTS candidate world transition
readback evidence VERIFIES target claim
</code>
<p>Facts make work eligible. Grants authorize effects. Never merge them.</p=
>



13. Runtime enforcement: QP must be the only path to consequence
<p>Create one effect gateway, e.g.:</p>

<code>await qp.effects.execute({
  proposal,
  required_claims,
  grant_id,
  adapter,
  readback_probe,
  target_proofspec,
});
</code>
<p>Direct provider-effect functions should become internal/private adapters=
 and must not be reachable from raw MCP dispatch.</p>
<p>These current functions must not execute directly from caller input:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>cfRegisterDomain</code></li>
<li><code>cfWireEmail</code></li>
<li><code>telnyxPurchaseNumber</code></li>
<li><code>email.send</code></li>
<li>future social/account mutation</li>
<li>OAuth write/credential changes</li>
<li>posting APIs</li>
</ul>
<p>MCP should create a proposal or submit authority; QP decides whether an =
effect may execute.</p>



14. Fix the current authentication/authority hole before anything else
<p>Current <code>/mcp</code> accepts caller <code>actor</code>, defaults it=
 to <code>owner</code>, and <code>owner</code> maps to ADMIN. That is not a=
cceptable for a system holding purchase/send/DNS capabilities.</p>
<p>Required changes:</p>
<ol>
<li>Authenticate every non-public MCP request using a real bearer/API-token=
/session credential.</li>
<li>Derive principal server-side from credential. Never trust caller-suppli=
ed <code>actor</code> as identity.</li>
<li>Remove default <code>owner</code> authority.</li>
<li>Separate read-only public tools from authenticated private tools.</li>
<li>Money/send/DNS/account write routes require QP signed grants in additio=
n to authentication.</li>
<li>Rate-limit and audit rejected grant/identity attempts.</li>
<li>Rotate any secrets if there is any possibility the current unauthentica=
ted route was deployed with consequential credentials enabled.</li>
</ol>
<p>Do this before feature work.</p>



